      "headline": "Development of Modern Fencing",
      "text": "The modern sport of fencing began to gain prominence near the end of the 19th century. It evolved from the traditional skill set of swordsmanship.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Italian School",
      "text": "The Italian school altered the historical European martial art of classical fencing, contributing significantly to the development of modern fencing techniques.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Refinement by the French School",
      "text": "The French school further refined the system of fencing, influencing the techniques and rules that are used in the sport today.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Inclusion in the First Modern Olympics",
      "text": "Fencing was included in the first modern Olympic Games held in Athens in 1896, featuring events for men in foil and sabre.",
      "date": "1896"
