      "headline": "Declaration of the State of Israel",
      "text": "On May 14, 1948, Ben-Gurion proclaimed the establishment of the State of Israel and became its first Prime Minister and Minister of Defense.",
      "date": "1948-05-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Magic Carpet",
      "text": "From June 1949 to September 1950, Ben-Gurion oversaw Operation Magic Carpet, which airlifted Yemenite Jews to Israel.",
      "date": "1949-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resignation as Prime Minister",
      "text": "In 1953, Ben-Gurion resigned as Prime Minister and retired to Kibbutz Sde Boker in the Negev desert.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Politics",
      "text": "Ben-Gurion returned to politics in 1955, serving again as Prime Minister and Minister of Defense.",
      "date": "1955"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Suez Crisis",
      "text": "In 1956, Ben-Gurion led Israel during the Suez Crisis, a military campaign against Egypt.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Final Resignation",
      "text": "Ben-Gurion resigned as Prime Minister for the final time in 1963, succeeded by Levi Eshkol.",
      "date": "1963"
    },
