      "headline": "Ratification of the Eighteenth Amendment",
      "text": "On January 16, 1919, the Eighteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution was ratified, prohibiting the production, importation, transportation, and sale of alcoholic beverages.",
      "date": "1919-01-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Volstead Act Passed",
      "text": "On October 28, 1919, the Volstead Act was passed by Congress, providing for the enforcement of the Eighteenth Amendment.",
      "date": "1919-10-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prohibition Begins",
      "text": "Prohibition officially began on January 17, 1920, when the Eighteenth Amendment went into effect, making the production, importation, transportation, and sale of alcoholic beverages illegal in the United States.",
      "date": "1920-01-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "St. Valentine's Day Massacre",
      "text": "On February 14, 1929, the St. Valentine's Day Massacre occurred in Chicago, highlighting the violent gang conflicts that arose during Prohibition.",
      "date": "1929-02-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ratification of the Twenty-first Amendment",
      "text": "On December 5, 1933, the Twenty-first Amendment was ratified, repealing the Eighteenth Amendment and effectively ending Prohibition in the United States.",
      "date": "1933-12-05"
    }
  ]
}

