      "text": "On October 3, 1990, the German Democratic Republic (East Germany) joined the Federal Republic of Germany, leading to the reunification of Germany. This resulted in the addition of five new states: Brandenburg, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, Saxony, Saxony-Anhalt, and Thuringia.",
