      "text": "In 1290, King Denis of Portugal created the first Portuguese university in Lisbon and declared Portuguese the official language of the kingdom, replacing Latin.",
      "date": "1290"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion during the Age of Discoveries",
      "text": "During the 15th and 16th centuries, Portuguese spread to Africa, Asia, and the Americas as Portugal established a global empire, leading to its status as a world language.",
