      "headline": "Founding of CBS",
      "text": "CBS was founded as United Independent Broadcasters Inc. in Chicago by Arthur Judson in January 1927.",
      "date": "1927-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acquisition by Columbia Phonograph Company",
      "text": "In April 1927, the Columbia Phonograph Company, parent of the Columbia record label, invested in the network, which was renamed the Columbia Phonographic Broadcasting System.",
      "date": "1927-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "William S. Paley's Acquisition",
      "text": "In 1928, William S. Paley purchased a majority interest in the network and became its president, renaming it the Columbia Broadcasting System.",
      "date": "1928"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CBS Radio Network Launch",
      "text": "CBS launched its radio network in 1928, which quickly grew to include 47 affiliates.",
      "date": "1928"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CBS Television Network Launch",
      "text": "CBS began its television network operations on July 1, 1941, with the first commercial broadcast.",
      "date": "1941-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Color Television",
      "text": "CBS made its first color television broadcast on June 25, 1951, although the system was not compatible with existing black-and-white sets.",
      "date": "1951-06-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CBS Acquires New York Yankees Broadcast Rights",
      "text": "In 1964, CBS acquired the broadcast rights to the New York Yankees, marking a significant expansion into sports broadcasting.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sale of CBS to Westinghouse Electric Corporation",
      "text": "In 1995, CBS was acquired by Westinghouse Electric Corporation, which later changed its name to CBS Corporation.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Merger with Viacom",
      "text": "In 2000, CBS Corporation merged with Viacom, forming a media conglomerate that included Paramount Pictures and MTV.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CBS and Viacom Split",
      "text": "In 2006, CBS Corporation and Viacom split into two separate companies, with CBS retaining the broadcasting and television production assets.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-merger with Viacom",
      "text": "In December 2019, CBS Corporation re-merged with Viacom to form ViacomCBS, later rebranded as Paramount Global.",
      "date": "2019-12"
