      "text": "In 1978, the Village People released the album 'Cruisin'', which featured the hit single 'Y.M.C.A.'. The song became one of the group's most famous tracks and a disco anthem.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Go West'",
      "text": "In 1979, the Village People released the album 'Go West', which included the popular title track. The album further cemented their status in the disco music scene.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'In the Navy'",
      "text": "In 1979, the Village People released the album 'Go West', which featured the hit single 'In the Navy'. The song became another major hit for the group.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Starring in 'Can't Stop the Music'",
      "text": "In 1980, the Village People starred in the musical comedy film 'Can't Stop the Music'. Although the film was not a commercial success, it has since gained a cult following.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victor Willis Departs",
      "text": "In 1980, lead singer Victor Willis left the Village People. His departure marked a significant change in the group's lineup.",
      "date": "1980"
