      "headline": "Discovery by Christopher Columbus",
      "text": "Montserrat was discovered by Christopher Columbus on his second voyage to the Americas in November 1493. He named the island after the Virgin of Montserrat in Spain.",
      "date": "1493-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First European Settlement",
      "text": "The first European settlers arrived in Montserrat in 1632. These were Irish Catholics who had been expelled from the nearby island of St. Kitts by the English.",
      "date": "1632"
    },
    {
      "headline": "French Occupation",
      "text": "The French briefly occupied Montserrat in 1664 and again in 1782, but the island was returned to British control under the Treaty of Paris in 1783.",
      "date": "1783"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abolition of Slavery",
      "text": "Slavery was abolished in Montserrat in 1834, following the Slavery Abolition Act passed by the British Parliament.",
      "date": "1834"
    },
