      "headline": "Soufrière Hills Volcano Eruption",
      "text": "The Soufrière Hills volcano began erupting in 1995, leading to the evacuation of the capital, Plymouth, and significant disruption to the island's population and economy.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction of Plymouth",
      "text": "In 1997, the Soufrière Hills volcano eruption destroyed the capital city of Plymouth, burying it under volcanic ash and forcing the relocation of the population.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of New Capital",
      "text": "Following the destruction of Plymouth, a new capital, Brades, was established in the northern part of the island.",
