      "headline": "Kyoto during the Edo Period",
      "text": "During the Edo period (1603-1868), Kyoto remained the cultural and religious center of Japan, despite the political power being held by the Tokugawa shogunate in Edo (Tokyo).",
      "date": "1603"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Meiji Restoration",
      "text": "In 1868, the Meiji Restoration led to the transfer of the capital from Kyoto to Tokyo, marking the end of Kyoto's status as the imperial capital.",
      "date": "1868"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kyoto spared during World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, Kyoto was spared from large-scale destruction and was not targeted by atomic bombings, preserving its historical and cultural heritage.",
      "date": "1945"
