      "headline": "Adoption of the Gregorian Calendar",
      "text": "In 1912, the Republic of China adopted the Gregorian calendar, but the Chinese New Year continued to be celebrated according to the traditional lunisolar calendar.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chinese New Year as a Public Holiday",
      "text": "In 1949, the People's Republic of China officially recognized Chinese New Year as a public holiday, emphasizing its cultural significance.",
