      "text": "On 21 October 1966, a colliery spoil tip collapsed on a mountain slope above the Welsh village of Aberfan, near Merthyr Tydfil. Heavy rain led to a build-up of water within the tip, causing it to slide downhill as a slurry. The disaster engulfed Pantglas Junior School and a row of houses, killing 116 children and 28 adults.",
