      "headline": "First Official Marathon World Record",
      "text": "The first official marathon world record was recognized by the International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF) in 1908. The record was set by Johnny Hayes of the United States with a time of 2:55:18.4 at the London Olympic Games.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Sub-2:30 Marathon",
      "text": "On October 24, 1925, Albert Michelsen of the United States became the first person to run a marathon in under 2 hours and 30 minutes, setting a new world record with a time of 2:29:01.8.",
