      "text": "Warner Bros. released The Jazz Singer, the first feature-length motion picture with synchronized dialogue sequences, marking the beginning of the sound era in film. This film premiered on October 6, 1927.",
      "date": "1927-10-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Looney Tunes",
      "text": "Warner Bros. introduced the Looney Tunes series, which became one of the most popular animated series in history. The first Looney Tunes cartoon, Sinkin' in the Bathtub, was released in 1930.",
      "date": "1930"
    },
