      "headline": "Seville's Golden Age",
      "text": "During the 16th century, Seville became one of the most important cities in the world due to its monopoly on trade with the Spanish colonies in the Americas.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Plague of Seville",
      "text": "In 1649, Seville was struck by a devastating plague that killed nearly half of its population.",
      "date": "1649"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Trade Monopoly",
      "text": "In 1717, the monopoly of trade with the Americas was transferred from Seville to Cádiz, leading to a decline in Seville's economic importance.",
      "date": "1717"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Seville's Industrialization",
      "text": "In the 19th century, Seville began to industrialize, which helped to revive its economy.",
      "date": "1800"
