      "headline": "Icebound in Victoria Strait",
      "text": "The expedition became icebound in Victoria Strait near King William Island in the Canadian Arctic, in what is today Nunavut. This occurred sometime in 1846.",
      "date": "1846"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abandonment of Ships",
      "text": "After being icebound for more than a year, HMS Erebus and HMS Terror were abandoned in April 1848. By this time, two dozen men, including Captain Sir John Franklin, had died.",
      "date": "1848-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Survivors Set Out for Canadian Mainland",
      "text": "The remaining crew, led by Franklin's second-in-command, Francis Crozier, and Erebus's captain, James Fitzjames, set out for the Canadian mainland. They disappeared and presumably perished.",
      "date": "1848"
