      "text": "On June 16, 2015, Donald Trump announced his candidacy for President of the United States, during which he proposed building a wall along the U.S.-Mexico border to curb illegal immigration.",
      "date": "2015-06-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trump Elected President",
      "text": "Donald Trump was elected as the 45th President of the United States on November 8, 2016. His campaign prominently featured the promise to build a wall along the southern border.",
      "date": "2016-11-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Executive Order Signed",
      "text": "On January 25, 2017, President Trump signed Executive Order 13767, directing the construction of a wall along the U.S.-Mexico border.",
      "date": "2017-01-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prototypes Built",
      "text": "In October 2017, the U.S. government completed the construction of eight border wall prototypes near San Diego, California, to evaluate different designs.",
      "date": "2017-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Government Shutdown Over Wall Funding",
      "text": "A partial government shutdown began on December 22, 2018, due to a standoff over funding for the border wall. It became the longest shutdown in U.S. history, lasting until January 25, 2019.",
      "date": "2018-12-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "National Emergency Declaration",
      "text": "On February 15, 2019, President Trump declared a national emergency to redirect funds from other federal projects to build the border wall after Congress refused to allocate the requested $5.7 billion.",
      "date": "2019-02-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Supreme Court Ruling",
      "text": "On July 26, 2019, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that the Trump administration could use $2.5 billion in Pentagon funds to build the border wall.",
      "date": "2019-07-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction Milestone",
      "text": "By January 2020, the Trump administration announced that 100 miles of new border wall had been completed.",
      "date": "2020-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Trump's Presidency",
      "text": "Donald Trump's presidency ended on January 20, 2021. By this time, approximately 452 miles of border wall had been constructed, mostly replacing existing barriers.",
      "date": "2021-01-20"
    }
  ]
}

