      "headline": "Adoption by the Romans",
      "text": "The Romans adopted the 12-hour clock system, which was used in their daily life and influenced the development of timekeeping in Western civilization.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Medieval European Use",
      "text": "During the medieval period, the 12-hour clock system was used in European monasteries to regulate prayer times.",
      "date": "1000"
    },
