      "text": "The M4 Sherman was gradually phased out of U.S. military service in the 1950s as newer tank models were developed.",
      "date": "1950"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "headline": "Founding of Sociology",
      "text": "Sociology as a distinct discipline was founded in the early 19th century. Auguste Comte, a French philosopher, is often credited with coining the term 'sociology' in 1838.",
      "date": "1838"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Communist Manifesto'",
      "text": "In 1848, Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels published 'The Communist Manifesto', which had a significant impact on sociology by introducing concepts of class struggle and social change.",
      "date": "1848"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Emile Durkheim's 'The Division of Labour in Society'",
      "text": "In 1893, Emile Durkheim published 'The Division of Labour in Society', which introduced the concept of social facts and laid the groundwork for functionalist theory.",
      "date": "1893"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Max Weber's 'The Protestant Ethic and the Spirit of Capitalism'",
      "text": "Max Weber published 'The Protestant Ethic and the Spirit of Capitalism' in 1905, which examined the relationship between religion and economic behavior.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the American Sociological Association",
      "text": "The American Sociological Association was founded in 1905 to promote the discipline of sociology in the United States.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Mind, Self and Society'",
      "text": "In 1934, George Herbert Mead's 'Mind, Self and Society' was published posthumously, contributing significantly to symbolic interactionism.",
      "date": "1934"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Talcott Parsons' 'The Structure of Social Action'",
      "text": "In 1937, Talcott Parsons published 'The Structure of Social Action', which introduced his theory of action and laid the foundation for structural functionalism.",
      "date": "1937"
    },
    {
      "headline": "C. Wright Mills' 'The Sociological Imagination'",
      "text": "In 1959, C. Wright Mills published 'The Sociological Imagination', which encouraged sociologists to connect personal experiences with larger social and historical forces.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Distinction: A Social Critique of the Judgement of Taste'",
      "text": "Pierre Bourdieu published 'Distinction: A Social Critique of the Judgement of Taste' in 1979, which explored the role of cultural capital in social stratification.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Postmodern Sociology",
      "text": "In the late 20th century, postmodern sociology emerged, challenging traditional narratives and emphasizing the fragmented and subjective nature of social reality.",
      "date": "1980"
    }
  ]
}

