      "text": "Herbert Maxwell Sobel was born on January 26, 1912, in Chicago, Illinois, United States.",
      "date": "1912-01-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Commissioned as an Officer",
      "text": "Herbert Sobel was commissioned as an officer in the United States Army, eventually serving with Easy Company, 2nd Battalion, 506th Parachute Infantry Regiment, 101st Airborne Division during World War II.",
      "date": "1942"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Training of Easy Company",
      "text": "Sobel was responsible for training the men of Easy Company at Camp Toccoa, Georgia, in preparation for their deployment in World War II.",
      "date": "1942"
    },
    {
      "headline": "D-Day and Normandy Invasion",
      "text": "Although Sobel did not participate in the D-Day parachute assault on Normandy, his training of Easy Company was crucial for their performance during the operation on June 6, 1944.",
      "date": "1944-06-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reassignment",
      "text": "Due to conflicts with his men and leadership style, Sobel was reassigned from Easy Company before the company's deployment to Europe.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
