      "headline": "USB 1.0 Specification Released",
      "text": "The USB 1.0 specification was released in January 1996. It was designed to replace a variety of legacy connectors with a single standardized interface.",
      "date": "1996-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "USB 1.1 Specification Released",
      "text": "In September 1998, the USB 1.1 specification was released, which fixed issues identified in USB 1.0 and was the first widely adopted version.",
      "date": "1998-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "USB 2.0 Specification Released",
      "text": "The USB 2.0 specification was released in April 2000, increasing the maximum data transfer rate to 480 Mbps, known as 'Hi-Speed USB'.",
      "date": "2000-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "USB 3.0 Specification Released",
      "text": "In November 2008, the USB 3.0 specification was released, introducing 'SuperSpeed USB' with a maximum data transfer rate of 5 Gbps.",
