      "headline": "Death of Arius",
      "text": "Arius died in 336 under mysterious circumstances, possibly due to poisoning.",
      "date": "0336"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Council of Constantinople",
      "text": "In 381, the First Council of Constantinople reaffirmed the Nicene Creed and further condemned Arianism.",
      "date": "0381"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of Arianism",
      "text": "By the end of the 4th century, Arianism began to decline significantly within the Roman Empire, although it persisted among some Germanic tribes.",
      "date": "0399"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conversion of the Visigoths",
      "text": "In 589, the Visigoths, who were Arian Christians, converted to Nicene Christianity at the Third Council of Toledo.",
