      "headline": "Initial Development of DisplayPort",
      "text": "DisplayPort was developed by a consortium of PC and chip manufacturers as a digital display interface. It was standardized by the Video Electronics Standards Association (VESA).",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of DisplayPort 1.0",
      "text": "DisplayPort 1.0 was released in May 2006. It introduced a new digital display interface standard that could carry video, audio, and other data.",
      "date": "2006-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of DisplayPort 1.1",
      "text": "In April 2007, DisplayPort 1.1 was introduced. This version added support for High-bandwidth Digital Content Protection (HDCP).",
      "date": "2007-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of DisplayPort 1.2",
      "text": "DisplayPort 1.2 was launched in December 2009. It doubled the data rate to 17.28 Gbit/s and introduced support for multiple monitors through a single connector.",
      "date": "2009-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of DisplayPort 1.3",
      "text": "DisplayPort 1.3 was released in September 2014. It increased the data rate to 32.4 Gbit/s and added support for 5K displays.",
      "date": "2014-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of DisplayPort 1.4",
      "text": "In March 2016, DisplayPort 1.4 was introduced. It included support for Display Stream Compression 1.2, HDR10, and improved audio capabilities.",
      "date": "2016-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Announcement of DisplayPort 2.0",
      "text": "DisplayPort 2.0 was announced in June 2019. It tripled the bandwidth to 77.4 Gbit/s and supported 8K resolution at 60Hz with HDR.",
      "date": "2019-06"
    }
  ]
}

