      "headline": "Introduction of the Affordable Care Act",
      "text": "The Affordable Care Act (ACA), also known as Obamacare, was introduced to the United States Congress. It aimed to expand healthcare coverage, control healthcare costs, and improve the healthcare delivery system.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Passage of the Affordable Care Act",
      "text": "The ACA was passed by the United States Senate on December 24, 2009, and by the House of Representatives on March 21, 2010.",
      "date": "2010-03-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Signing into Law",
      "text": "President Barack Obama signed the Affordable Care Act into law on March 23, 2010. This marked a significant overhaul of the U.S. healthcare system.",
      "date": "2010-03-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Health Care and Education Reconciliation Act",
      "text": "The Health Care and Education Reconciliation Act of 2010, which amended the ACA, was signed into law by President Obama on March 30, 2010.",
      "date": "2010-03-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Supreme Court Upholds ACA",
      "text": "On June 28, 2012, the U.S. Supreme Court upheld the constitutionality of the ACA's individual mandate as a tax in the landmark case National Federation of Independent Business v. Sebelius.",
      "date": "2012-06-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of Health Insurance Marketplaces",
      "text": "The ACA's health insurance marketplaces opened on October 1, 2013, allowing individuals to purchase health insurance plans.",
      "date": "2013-10-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Open Enrollment Period",
      "text": "The first open enrollment period for the ACA's health insurance marketplaces began on October 1, 2013, and ended on March 31, 2014.",
      "date": "2013-10-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "King v. Burwell Decision",
      "text": "On June 25, 2015, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled in King v. Burwell that federal subsidies for health insurance were legal in states that did not set up their own exchanges.",
      "date": "2015-06-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Repeal of Individual Mandate Penalty",
      "text": "The Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, signed into law on December 22, 2017, repealed the ACA's individual mandate penalty, effective in 2019.",
      "date": "2017-12-22"
    }
  ]
}

