      "headline": "Publication of the Georgics",
      "text": "In 29 BCE, Virgil completed the Georgics, a didactic poem in four books, which focuses on agriculture and rural life.",
      "date": "-0029"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Work on the Aeneid",
      "text": "Virgil began working on the Aeneid, an epic poem that tells the story of Aeneas, a Trojan who traveled to Italy and became an ancestor of the Romans, around 29 BCE.",
      "date": "-0029"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Virgil",
      "text": "Virgil died on September 21, 19 BCE, in Brundisium (modern Brindisi), Italy. He left the Aeneid unfinished.",
      "date": "-0019-09-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Posthumous Publication of the Aeneid",
      "text": "Despite Virgil's dying wish to have the Aeneid destroyed, Augustus ordered its publication. The poem was published posthumously in 19 BCE.",
      "date": "-0019"
    }
  ]
}

