    {
      "headline": "Widespread Use in Anesthesia",
      "text": "Throughout the 1990s and 2000s, Propofol became widely used for the induction and maintenance of general anesthesia, as well as for sedation in intensive care units.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Generic Versions Released",
      "text": "Following the expiration of the original patent, numerous generic versions of Propofol were released, increasing its availability and use worldwide.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
