      "headline": "Ratification of the Second Amendment",
      "text": "The Second Amendment to the United States Constitution was ratified on December 15, 1791, as part of the Bill of Rights, which includes ten amendments.",
      "date": "1791-12-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "District of Columbia v. Heller",
      "text": "In 2008, the Supreme Court case District of Columbia v. Heller affirmed for the first time that the Second Amendment protects an individual's right to possess a firearm for self-defense within the home. The decision also noted that the right is not unlimited and does not preclude certain prohibitions.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
      "headline": "McDonald v. City of Chicago",
      "text": "In 2010, the Supreme Court ruled in McDonald v. City of Chicago that the Second Amendment applies to state and local governments, limiting them in the same way as the federal government from infringing upon the right to keep and bear arms.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "New York State Rifle & Pistol Association, Inc. v. Bruen",
      "text": "In 2022, the Supreme Court case New York State Rifle & Pistol Association, Inc. v. Bruen assured the right to carry weapons in public spaces, with reasonable exceptions.",
      "date": "2022"
    }
  ]
}

