      "text": "In 1975, Mugabe became the leader of ZANU after a leadership struggle within the party.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lancaster House Agreement",
      "text": "In December 1979, Mugabe participated in the Lancaster House Agreement, which led to the end of white-minority rule in Rhodesia.",
      "date": "1979-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mugabe Becomes Prime Minister",
      "text": "On April 18, 1980, Mugabe became the Prime Minister of Zimbabwe following the country's independence.",
      "date": "1980-04-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mugabe Becomes President",
      "text": "In 1987, Mugabe transitioned from Prime Minister to President of Zimbabwe, a position he held until 2017.",
