      "headline": "Formation of the Khazar Khaganate",
      "text": "The Khazar Khaganate was established in the late 6th century CE, following the collapse of the Western Turkic Khaganate. The Khazars emerged as a dominant power in the region, controlling territories in modern-day European Russia, southern Ukraine, Crimea, and Kazakhstan.",
      "date": "0560"
