      "headline": "Khazar-Arab Wars",
      "text": "Throughout the 7th and 8th centuries, the Khazars engaged in a series of conflicts with the Arab Caliphates, known as the Khazar-Arab Wars. These conflicts were primarily over control of the Caucasus region.",
      "date": "0700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of Khazar Power",
      "text": "During the 9th century, the Khazar Khaganate reached the height of its power, controlling key trade routes and acting as a major commercial hub between the East and West.",
      "date": "0900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of the Khazar Khaganate",
      "text": "By the late 10th century, the Khazar Khaganate began to decline due to internal strife, external pressures from the Rus' and other emerging powers, and the shifting trade routes.",
      "date": "0970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fall of the Khazar Khaganate",
      "text": "In 965 CE, the Khazar Khaganate was decisively defeated by Sviatoslav I of Kiev, marking the end of Khazar dominance in the region.",
      "date": "0965"
    }
  ]
}

