      "headline": "Operation Barbarossa Begins",
      "text": "On 22 June 1941, Nazi Germany launched Operation Barbarossa, the invasion of the Soviet Union, marking the beginning of the Eastern Front in World War II.",
      "date": "1941-06-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Siege of Leningrad Begins",
      "text": "The Siege of Leningrad began on 8 September 1941, lasting for 872 days until 27 January 1944, resulting in severe famine and casualties.",
      "date": "1941-09-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Moscow",
      "text": "The Battle of Moscow took place from October 1941 to January 1942, where Soviet forces successfully defended the city against the German advance.",
      "date": "1941-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Stalingrad",
      "text": "The Battle of Stalingrad occurred from 23 August 1942 to 2 February 1943, ending with a decisive Soviet victory and turning point in the war.",
      "date": "1942-08-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Kursk",
      "text": "The Battle of Kursk, from 5 July to 23 August 1943, was the largest tank battle in history and resulted in a significant Soviet victory.",
      "date": "1943-07-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Siege of Leningrad Ends",
      "text": "The Siege of Leningrad was lifted on 27 January 1944, after a successful Soviet offensive.",
      "date": "1944-01-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Bagration",
      "text": "Operation Bagration, launched on 22 June 1944, was a massive Soviet offensive that destroyed the German Army Group Centre.",
      "date": "1944-06-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Vistula–Oder Offensive",
      "text": "The Vistula–Oder Offensive, from 12 January to 2 February 1945, saw Soviet forces advance into German-held territory, reaching the Oder River.",
      "date": "1945-01-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Berlin",
      "text": "The Battle of Berlin, from 16 April to 2 May 1945, resulted in the capture of Berlin by Soviet forces and the suicide of Adolf Hitler.",
      "date": "1945-04-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victory in Europe Day",
      "text": "On 9 May 1945, the Eastern Front officially ended with the unconditional surrender of Nazi Germany, marking Victory in Europe Day.",
