      "headline": "First Inhabitants",
      "text": "The area now known as South Dakota was inhabited by various indigenous peoples for thousands of years before European contact. The Dakota Sioux became the dominant tribe in the region.",
      "date": "-10000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Louisiana Purchase",
      "text": "In 1803, the United States acquired the land that would become South Dakota from France as part of the Louisiana Purchase.",
