      "headline": "Treaty of Fort Laramie",
      "text": "In 1851, the Treaty of Fort Laramie was signed, establishing boundaries for Native American territories, including parts of present-day South Dakota.",
      "date": "1851"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dakota Territory Established",
      "text": "In 1861, the Dakota Territory was established, encompassing the present-day states of North Dakota, South Dakota, and parts of Montana and Wyoming.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Black Hills Gold Rush",
      "text": "In 1874, gold was discovered in the Black Hills, leading to a gold rush and increased settlement in the area.",
      "date": "1874"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Sioux War",
      "text": "From 1876 to 1877, the Great Sioux War occurred, resulting in the U.S. government seizing control of the Black Hills from the Sioux.",
      "date": "1876"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Statehood",
      "text": "On November 2, 1889, South Dakota was admitted to the Union as the 40th state.",
      "date": "1889-11-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mount Rushmore Completed",
      "text": "In 1941, the Mount Rushmore National Memorial was completed, featuring the carved faces of four U.S. presidents.",
