      "text": "Nice was founded around 350 BCE by the Greeks of Massalia (modern Marseille) and was given the name Nikaia in honor of a victory over the neighboring Ligurians.",
      "date": "-0350"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Era",
      "text": "During the Roman era, Nice became an important trading post and was part of the Roman province of Alpes Maritimae.",
      "date": "-0015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Middle Ages",
      "text": "In the Middle Ages, Nice was part of the County of Provence and later came under the control of the House of Savoy in 1388.",
      "date": "1388"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by France",
      "text": "Nice was annexed by France in 1860 following the Treaty of Turin, which was a result of the Second Italian War of Independence.",
      "date": "1860"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, Nice was occupied by Italian and later German forces. It was liberated by the Allies in 1944.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Development",
      "text": "In the post-war period, Nice developed into a major tourist destination and cultural hub on the French Riviera.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2016 Nice Attack",
      "text": "On July 14, 2016, a terrorist attack occurred in Nice when a truck was deliberately driven into crowds celebrating Bastille Day, resulting in 86 deaths and many injuries.",
      "date": "2016-07-14"
    }
  ]
}

