      "headline": "Origin of Jujutsu",
      "text": "Jujutsu originated in Japan as a method of close combat for defeating an armed and armored opponent in which one uses no weapon, or only a short weapon. The earliest recorded use of the term 'jujutsu' was in the 17th century.",
      "date": "1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the First Jujutsu School",
      "text": "Hisamori Tenenuchi officially established the first school of jiu-jitsu in Japan, marking the formalization of jujutsu as a martial art.",
