      "headline": "Origin of the House of Bourbon",
      "text": "The House of Bourbon originated in 1272 when Robert, the youngest son of King Louis IX of France, married Beatrice of Burgundy, the heiress of the lordship of Bourbon.",
      "date": "1272"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bourbon Becomes a Cadet Branch",
      "text": "For three centuries, the House of Bourbon continued as a cadet branch, serving as nobles under the direct Capetian and Valois kings.",
      "date": "1300"
