      "headline": "First Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "The first Impressionist exhibition was held in Paris from April 15 to May 15, 1874. It was organized by the Société Anonyme Coopérative des Artistes Peintres, Sculpteurs, Graveurs, and included works by artists such as Claude Monet, Edgar Degas, and Pierre-Auguste Renoir.",
      "date": "1874-04-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "The second Impressionist exhibition took place in Paris from April 1 to May 15, 1876. This exhibition included works by artists like Berthe Morisot and Gustave Caillebotte, further establishing the movement.",
      "date": "1876-04-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Third Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "Held from April 10 to May 11, 1877, the third Impressionist exhibition featured notable works by Claude Monet, including his famous series of paintings of the Gare Saint-Lazare.",
      "date": "1877-04-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fourth Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "The fourth exhibition took place from April 10 to May 11, 1879. It was marked by the participation of Mary Cassatt, an American artist who became an important figure in the movement.",
      "date": "1879-04-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fifth Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "This exhibition was held from April 1 to April 30, 1880, and included works by Edgar Degas, who played a significant role in organizing the event.",
      "date": "1880-04-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sixth Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "The sixth exhibition took place from April 2 to April 30, 1881. It featured works by Camille Pissarro and introduced new artists to the movement.",
      "date": "1881-04-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Seventh Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "Held from March 1 to March 30, 1882, the seventh exhibition included works by Claude Monet and Pierre-Auguste Renoir, showcasing the continued evolution of the Impressionist style.",
      "date": "1882-03-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eighth and Final Impressionist Exhibition",
      "text": "The eighth and final Impressionist exhibition occurred from May 15 to June 15, 1886. It marked the end of the formal exhibitions by the group, although the influence of Impressionism continued to grow.",
