      "headline": "Ancient Greece and Rome",
      "text": "In ancient Greece and Rome, euthanasia was practiced and accepted in some cases. However, the Hippocratic Oath, which originated around the 5th century BCE, explicitly prohibited doctors from giving a deadly drug to anyone, even if asked.",
      "date": "-0500"
