      "headline": "Kraków Occupied by Austria",
      "text": "In 1795, during the Third Partition of Poland, Kraków was annexed by the Austrian Empire.",
      "date": "1795"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Free City of Kraków",
      "text": "In 1815, the Congress of Vienna established Kraków as a Free City, a semi-independent city-state under the protection of Austria, Prussia, and Russia.",
      "date": "1815"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Incorporation into the Austrian Empire",
      "text": "In 1846, following a failed uprising, Kraków was annexed by the Austrian Empire and became part of the Kingdom of Galicia and Lodomeria.",
      "date": "1846"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kraków Becomes Part of Reborn Poland",
      "text": "In 1918, after World War I, Kraków became part of the newly independent Second Polish Republic.",
      "date": "1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nazi Occupation of Kraków",
      "text": "In 1939, during World War II, Nazi Germany occupied Kraków and made it the capital of the General Government.",
      "date": "1939"
