      "headline": "Outbreak of the Algerian War",
      "text": "The Algerian War began on November 1, 1954, when the National Liberation Front (FLN) launched a series of attacks against French military and civilian targets in Algeria.",
      "date": "1954-11-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Algiers",
      "text": "The Battle of Algiers took place from 1956 to 1957. It was a campaign of urban guerrilla warfare carried out by the FLN against the French authorities in the Algerian capital.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sétif and Guelma Massacre",
      "text": "In May 1945, the Sétif and Guelma massacre occurred, where French authorities killed thousands of Algerians. This event is often seen as a precursor to the Algerian War.",
      "date": "1945-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Philippeville Massacre",
      "text": "On August 20, 1955, the FLN attacked the town of Philippeville, leading to a brutal French crackdown and the massacre of thousands of Algerians.",
      "date": "1955-08-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "General Strike",
      "text": "On January 28, 1957, the FLN called for a general strike in Algiers to coincide with the United Nations debate on Algeria.",
      "date": "1957-01-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "De Gaulle's Visit to Algeria",
      "text": "On June 4, 1958, Charles de Gaulle visited Algeria and delivered his famous speech, 'Je vous ai compris' ('I have understood you'), signaling a shift in French policy.",
      "date": "1958-06-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Evian Accords",
      "text": "The Evian Accords were signed on March 18, 1962, between France and the FLN, leading to a ceasefire and paving the way for Algerian independence.",
      "date": "1962-03-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Algerian Independence",
      "text": "Algeria officially gained independence from France on July 5, 1962, following a referendum in which the Algerian people overwhelmingly voted for independence.",
      "date": "1962-07-05"
    }
  ]
}

