      "headline": "Facebook F8 2008",
      "text": "The second F8 conference took place on July 23, 2008. Facebook announced the Facebook Connect feature, allowing users to log into third-party websites using their Facebook credentials.",
      "date": "2008-07-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2010",
      "text": "Held on April 21, 2010, this F8 conference introduced the Open Graph API and the 'Like' button, which allowed users to share content from other websites on their Facebook profiles.",
      "date": "2010-04-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2011",
      "text": "On September 22, 2011, Facebook announced the Timeline feature, which replaced the traditional user profile with a more visual and chronological display of a user's history on the platform.",
      "date": "2011-09-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2014",
      "text": "After a three-year hiatus, the F8 conference returned on April 30, 2014. Facebook introduced the Audience Network, a mobile ad network, and announced anonymous login options for apps.",
      "date": "2014-04-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2015",
      "text": "The 2015 F8 conference was held on March 25, 2015. Key announcements included the Messenger Platform, allowing developers to build apps that integrate with Facebook Messenger.",
      "date": "2015-03-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2016",
      "text": "On April 12, 2016, Facebook announced several new features, including the launch of the Facebook Surround 360 camera and updates to the Messenger Platform, including chatbots.",
      "date": "2016-04-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2017",
      "text": "Held on April 18, 2017, this conference introduced the Camera Effects Platform, augmented reality tools, and Facebook Spaces, a virtual reality app for the Oculus Rift.",
      "date": "2017-04-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2018",
      "text": "The F8 conference on May 1, 2018, focused on privacy and security, with announcements about new privacy controls and the introduction of the Clear History feature.",
      "date": "2018-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2019",
      "text": "On April 30, 2019, Facebook unveiled a redesign of the platform, known as FB5, and announced new features for Messenger, Instagram, and WhatsApp.",
      "date": "2019-04-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 2020",
      "text": "The 2020 F8 conference was canceled due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Facebook opted for online announcements instead.",
      "date": "2020"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Facebook F8 Refresh 2021",
      "text": "On June 2, 2021, Facebook held a virtual event called F8 Refresh, focusing on new tools for developers and updates to the Messenger API.",
