      "text": "In 605 CE, the Quraysh tribe reconstructed the Kaaba. During this reconstruction, the Black Stone was temporarily removed and later replaced by the Prophet Muhammad, who resolved a dispute among the Quraysh by placing the stone on a cloth and having representatives of each clan lift it together.",
      "date": "0605"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Siege of Mecca",
      "text": "In 683 CE, during the siege of Mecca by the Umayyad army, the Kaaba was damaged by fire and the Black Stone was broken into several pieces.",
      "date": "0683"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Qarmatian Theft",
      "text": "In 930 CE, the Qarmatians, a sect of Ismaili Shia Islam, sacked Mecca and took the Black Stone to their base in Hajar (modern-day Bahrain). It was returned in 952 CE.",
      "date": "0930"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return of the Black Stone",
      "text": "The Black Stone was returned to Mecca in 952 CE after being held by the Qarmatians for over 20 years.",
      "date": "0952"
    }
  ]
}

