      "text": "In the 18th century, Leonhard Euler made significant contributions to the understanding of logarithms, including the introduction of the constant e, which is the base of natural logarithms.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Logarithms in Calculus",
      "text": "In the 18th century, logarithms became an essential tool in calculus, particularly in solving differential equations and in the study of exponential growth and decay.",
      "date": "1700"
    }
  ]
}

