      "headline": "Lion Air Flight 610 Crash",
      "text": "On October 29, 2018, Lion Air Flight 610 crashed into the Java Sea shortly after takeoff, killing all 189 people on board.",
      "date": "2018-10-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ethiopian Airlines Flight 302 Crash",
      "text": "On March 10, 2019, Ethiopian Airlines Flight 302 crashed shortly after takeoff, killing all 157 people on board.",
      "date": "2019-03-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Initial FAA Statement on Airworthiness",
      "text": "In the days following the Ethiopian Airlines crash, the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) initially affirmed the Boeing 737 MAX's continued airworthiness, citing insufficient evidence of accident similarities.",
      "date": "2019-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Grounding of Boeing 737 MAX",
      "text": "By March 13, 2019, the FAA decided to ground the Boeing 737 MAX, following the lead of 51 other regulators. All 387 aircraft delivered to airlines were grounded by March 18, 2019.",
      "date": "2019-03-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Initial Grounding",
      "text": "The Boeing 737 MAX was cleared to return to service in December 2020 after extensive reviews and modifications.",
      "date": "2020-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Grounding in 2024",
      "text": "The Boeing 737 MAX was grounded again in 2024 due to unspecified reasons.",
      "date": "2024"
    }
  ]
}

