      "headline": "Formulation of Fermi-Dirac Statistics",
      "text": "In 1926, Fermi formulated the Fermi-Dirac statistics, which describes the distribution of particles over energy states in systems consisting of many identical particles that obey the Pauli exclusion principle.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nobel Prize in Physics",
      "text": "In 1938, Enrico Fermi was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics for his work on induced radioactivity by neutron bombardment and for the discovery of transuranium elements.",
